{"name":"Satin Flower","hex":"#b48fbd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"satin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cloth woven from silk, nylon or polyester with a glossy surface and a dull back. (The same weaving technique applied to cotton produces cloth termed sateen).","Gin (the drink)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Semigloss."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satin"},{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Satin","blocks":[{"text":"A satin weave is a type of fabric weave that produces a characteristically glossy, smooth or lustrous material, typically with a glossy top surface and a dull back; it is not durable, as it tends to snag. It is one of three fundamental types of textile weaves alongside plain weave and twill weave."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Satin_weave_in_silk_90.jpg/330px-Satin_weave_in_silk_90.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satin"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Satin_bedding.jpg/500px-Satin_bedding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Satin_bedding.jpg/500px-Satin_bedding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Purple satin fabric","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASatin_bedding.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/1884_reception_dress%2C_silk_satin_and_brocade_with_chenille_fringe_08.jpg/500px-1884_reception_dress%2C_silk_satin_and_brocade_with_chenille_fringe_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/1884_reception_dress%2C_silk_satin_and_brocade_with_chenille_fringe_08.jpg/500px-1884_reception_dress%2C_silk_satin_and_brocade_with_chenille_fringe_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dress made from satin.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1884_reception_dress%2C_silk_satin_and_brocade_with_chenille_fringe_08.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Robe_a_la_Fran%C3%A7aise_c._1765.jpg/500px-Robe_a_la_Fran%C3%A7aise_c._1765.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Robe_a_la_Fran%C3%A7aise_c._1765.jpg/1280px-Robe_a_la_Fran%C3%A7aise_c._1765.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped